  "slides": [
    {
      "page_title": "Embedding: One Document, One Read",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`$push`, `$pull`, `$addToSet`, `$pop` for membership",
            "`$push` with `$each`/`$slice`/`$sort` keeps a capped top-N",
            "Array indexes are multikey: one entry per element",
            "A multikey index cannot be a shard key",
            "Only one array field per compound index"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "When To Embed"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "The relation is one-to-few",
            "The child has no independent lifecycle",
            "You always read the child with the parent",
            "Atomicity is free — no session or transaction API"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Bill For Embedding",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Duplicated data when the child is shared",
            "Bigger documents mean more I/O per read",
            "Unbounded growth walks toward the 16 MB wall",
            "Repeated growth makes WiredTiger rewrite the whole record"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "db.p.find({}, { items: { $slice: 10 } })",
            "// only the first 10 array elements"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Projection Tames Size",
          "text": "`$slice` in a projection keeps a fat embedded array off the wire when the page only shows ten."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Referencing stores a pointer — usually the target's `_id` — and resolves it with a second query or a `$lookup`."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Two Link Styles",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "cards",
          "spec": {
            "cards": [
              {
                "title": "Manual ref",
                "lines": [
                  "`{ authorId: ObjectId(...) }`",
                  "App knows the collection",
                  "The recommended default"
                ]
              },
              {
                "title": "DBRef",
                "lines": [
                  "`{ $ref, $id, $db }`",
                  "Self-describing",
                  "Driver must dereference",
                  "Rarely worth it"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Joining With `$lookup`",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "{ $lookup: { from: \"authors\",",
            "    localField: \"authorId\",",
            "    foreignField: \"_id\",",
            "    as: \"author\" } }   // always an array"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Follow with `$unwind` to flatten the array",
            "`preserveNullAndEmptyArrays` gives a true left join",
            "Index the `foreignField` or it scans per input doc",
            "An unindexed `$lookup` is an O(n·m) disaster",
            "The `let` + `pipeline` form allows correlated joins"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Referencing: Linking Documents",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Recursive Walks"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "{ $graphLookup: { from: \"emp\",",
            "  startWith: \"$managerId\",",
            "  connectFromField: \"managerId\",",
            "  connectToField: \"_id\",",
            "  as: \"chain\", maxDepth: 5 } }"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Walks org charts, category trees, follower graphs",
            "`maxDepth` bounds it, `depthField` tags each hop"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "When To Reference",
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "One-to-many with an unbounded many side",
            "The child is large",
            "The child is shared and must stay consistent in one place",
            "Child-to-parent scales better than an array of children",
            "The array is the thing that grows without bound"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Price Of Pointers",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A round trip, or a join stage, on every read",
            "No cross-document atomicity by default",
            "Two-way refs speed both directions but drift apart"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "session.withTransaction(async () => {",
            "  await a.updateOne(/* ... */);",
            "  await b.updateOne(/* ... */);  // 60s cap",
            "});"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Transactions Are The Exception",
          "text": "Multi-document transactions cost performance and time out at 60 seconds by default. Design so you rarely reach for one."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Governing Rule",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Data accessed together should be stored together",
            "Model for your queries, not for your entities",
            "An entity diagram describes the world, not the workload"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Cardinality Decides",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flowchart",
