    {
      "page_title": "Choosing A Model: Trade-offs & Patterns",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A user's three addresses: embed",
            "A post's bounded comments: embed with a cap",
            "Log lines: reference from the child side",
            "Join collection when the relation has its own fields"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Embed Versus Reference"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Axis",
            "Embed",
            "Reference"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "read",
              "1 read",
              "2 reads or `$lookup`"
            ],
            [
              "write",
              "1 atomic write",
              "2 writes + txn"
            ],
            [
              "duplication",
              "copies shared data",
              "stored once"
            ],
            [
              "growth",
              "capped at 16 MB",
              "unbounded"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Named Patterns",
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Pattern",
            "The move"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "extended ref",
              "hot fields copied into child"
            ],
            [
              "subset",
              "top 10 inline, rest aside"
            ],
            [
              "computed",
              "keep `commentCount`, `$inc` it"
            ],
            [
              "bucket",
              "per-hour time-series docs"
            ],
            [
              "outlier",
              "overflow flag + spill collection"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "{ postId: 9, body: \"...\",",
            "  author: { _id: 3, name: \"Ada\" } }",
            "// common read needs no join"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Migrating Shapes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Keep a `schemaVersion` field on every document",
            "Old and new shapes coexist through a rolling migration",
            "Readers branch on it, writers emit the new shape"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "When Duplication Wins",
          "items": [
            "The copied data rarely changes",
            "A join on every read beats a rare fan-out update — badly",
            "Bucketing cuts document count and index size hugely"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Outliers Are Real",
          "text": "The celebrity with 10M followers is 0.1% of your rows and 100% of your incidents. Flag and spill them."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Silent Empty Results",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "db.c.find({ _id: \"65f1a3b4c2d1e0f9a8b7c6d5\" })",
            "// [] — a string never matches ObjectId",
            "db.c.find({ age: { $gt: 30 } })",
            "// never matches age stored as \"31\""
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A type mismatch returns nothing, not an error",
            "Cast on the way in, at the app edge",
            "Cross-type comparison follows the BSON type order"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Numbers And Time",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Money as a double loses precision: `0.1 + 0.2 !== 0.3`",
            "Use `NumberDecimal` or integer minor units (cents)",
            "The shell makes every bare number a double",
            "`NumberInt`/`NumberLong` when the stored type matters",
            "Dates carry no zone: store UTC, render at the edge"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Gotchas, Pitfalls & Recap",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Null Versus Missing",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "db.c.find({ x: null })",
            "// matches missing AND explicit null",
            "db.c.find({ x: { $exists: true, $eq: null } })",
            "// only an explicit null"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Model Smells"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Unbounded arrays are the number one model failure",
            "Every array needs an answer to 'how big can this get?'",
            "Long field names cost bytes in every document",
            "Dots and `$` are legal since 5.0 and still break tooling",
            "Past 3-4 levels, positional updates get painful"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Slow Aggregation Checklist",
          "items": [
            "An unindexed `$lookup` field is the usual culprit",
            "Confirm with `explain(\"executionStats\")`",
            "Prefer manual references over `DBRef` indirection"
          ],
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Handbook In Four Lines",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "BSON is the binary, typed, length-prefixed reality behind the JSON",
            "`_id` is the mandatory, immutable, uniquely indexed key",
            "ObjectId is a 12-byte, time-ordered, client-minted default",
            "Swap it for a natural key whenever one exists"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "16 MB is a hard ceiling that punishes unbounded growth",
            "Bucket, subset or offload to object storage first",
            "Embed for locality and atomicity",
            "Reference for unbounded or shared data"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Duplicate a field, or join on every read?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "Duplicate, when the copy rarely changes",
            "The join usually costs more than the fan-out update",
            "Measure with `explain`, then duplicate deliberately"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Let The Queries Decide",
          "text": "Query patterns, not entity diagrams, pick your model."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "caption": {
    "text": "Part 2 of MONGODB INTERNALS. A MongoDB document is not JSON — it is BSON: binary, typed and length-prefixed, with a 16 MB ceiling that quietly punishes every unbounded array you ever wrote. This handbook takes the document apart byte by byte: the type zoo, the 12 bytes inside an ObjectId, why `_id` cannot be an array, and the real rules for embedding versus referencing. Ten pages of dense notes on the one thing every MongoDB decision rests on.",
